--- body ---
## Context
All four reviewers: the front matter (abstract, intro, conclusion) claims more
than the experiments measure. (a) the benchmark is presented as "reusable" while
methods were tuned in-sample on N=1 (Vietnam); (b) provenance is "verifiable not
verified" and external coherence is unmeasured, yet the paper implies full
data-quality scoring; (c) the contamination-as-ceiling design makes it closer to
a dated capability audit than a reusable benchmark. The §8 caveats already
exist — the fix is to surface them into the front matter and scope the claims.
Tracker: 0644. Reviews: openai_grinchy (obj 1,9), mistral_grinchy (obj 1,9),
openai_student (concern 1,3; §1).

## Action
- In abstract+intro+conclusion, scope "computable/reusable benchmark" to
  "demonstrated on the Vietnam case; cross-context transfer is future work".
- Relabel q3/q4 score components as proxy metrics (provenance = citation
  presence/verifiable, not verified; temporality shallow); state external
  coherence is not measured.
- Record the standing decisions in `docs/editorial-brief.md`; keep edits as
  negative-guard-safe surfacing (CI polarity rule).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Front matter no longer implies out-of-distribution validity or full 4-dimension scoring
- [ ] editorial-brief.md entries added; manuscript builds; adherence tests pass
